{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>That was on the hand of the other.</b> Four 'hands' are written here, corresponding to four banned things that Achan trespassed with, which came forth from him. And some say: corresponding to four things he took — the mantle of Shinar, two pieces of silver of two hundred shekels, and a tongue of gold. Bereshit Rabbah." "<b>And he called his name Zerach.</b> After the shining forth of the crimson thread."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:40.953113769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}